OL,3,GNEWSARolls-Royce gas leak caused by
OL,4,Aroutine bottle change
OL,5,
OL,6,FA gas leak at a Rolls-Royce factory
OL,7,Fstarted after a routine bottle
OL,8,Freplacement, the firm has said.
OL,10,FDerbyshire Fire and Rescue Service was
OL,11,Fcalled to the site in Raynesway at
OL,12,Fabout 15:40 GMT on Thursday. A 300m
OL,13,F(985ft) cordon was put in place and
OL,14,Flocals were asked to remain indoors
OL,15,Fwith windows and doors shut, however,
OL,16,Fthe guidance was lifted shortly before
OL,17,F22:00 GMT.
OL,19,FRolls-Royce Submarines reiterated the
OL,20,Fincident was "not a nuclear incident",
OL,21,Fwith employees moving to a nearby
OL,22,Fbuilding while it was resolved.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
